activate with no event handler must trap

The dts case libxpc connection_api_misuse_no_event_handler installs a signal handler, creates a
mach service connection, sets NO event handler and activates. On macOS that is API misuse and the
library traps, so the handler runs and the case exits 0. Ours forwarded straight to activate with
no check, the case fell through to its own abort, and the batch read 134.

__builtin_trap covers both arms with no ifdef: ud2 on x86_64 raises SIGILL, brk on arm64 raises
SIGTRAP, which is exactly the pair the case tests for.

The trap fires on ACTIVATE, not on create. The case asserts the connection is non NULL first, so
creating one without a handler still has to succeed.

EVERY IN TREE CALLER WAS READ, not sampled, because a trap here could kill a daemon. All ten set
the handler immediately before activating, which is the pattern macOS requires, so nothing existing
changes behaviour: security SOSCloudKeychainClient.c 202, otpaird OTPairingClient.m 24 and main.m
96 and 98, trustd.c 802 and 806, mDNSResponder dnssd.c 1188, dnssd_server.c 456 and 686,
helper-stubs.c 77. trustd is the one that matters most, since MoneyMoney depends on it.

It names the service before trapping. A bare ud2 inside a daemon reads as an unattributed crash,
and that exact ambiguity is what made task #197 look intermittent for a long time.

--- a/src/connection.m
+++ b/src/connection.m
@@ -1504,6 +1504,16 @@
 XPC_EXPORT
 void xpc_connection_activate(xpc_connection_t xconn) {
 	TO_OBJC_CHECKED(connection, xconn, conn) {
+		/* Activating with no event handler is API misuse and macOS traps on it. __builtin_trap
+		 * emits ud2 on x86_64, raising SIGILL, and brk on arm64, raising SIGTRAP, which is the
+		 * pair callers catch. Name the service first: a bare ud2 inside a daemon looks like an
+		 * unattributed crash, and that ambiguity cost days on task #197. */
+		if (![conn eventHandler]) {
+			const char* name = [conn serviceName];
+			fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_XPC API MISUSE: xpc_connection_activate on %s with no event handler\n",
+			        name ? name : "an anonymous connection");
+			__builtin_trap();
+		}
 		if ([conn activate]) {
 			[conn decrementSuspensionCount];
 		}
